## Part 11 — Planned extensions

### 11.1 The extension ladder (in order)

1. **Signed second shift term.** `a − b` as well as `a + b`. This fills in 7, 11, 13, 14, 15 and makes clean uniform ramps expressible. Costs a subtract capability in the adder, which is cheap.
2. **Wider shifts.** Extend the term set beyond {1,2,4,8}.
3. **Third term.** Depth-2 tree, giving up the core structural advantage — only if accuracy demands it.
4. **Exact O(KN²) dynamic-programming codebook search.** Replaces the exhaustive-over-legal-sets search with an optimal DP, useful once the legal family grows too large to enumerate.
5. **Lagrangian bit allocation for mixed precision.** Choose per-layer bit-widths under a global budget.

### 11.2 Low-rank residual branch

Adding an FP16 `U·Vᵀ` correction on top of the quantized weights (the CALDERA / LQER / QuIP# family) has been confirmed to **compose cleanly** with the BoA pipeline via alternating optimization on the residual.

**The mandatory caveat: honest effective-bits accounting.** A W2 model plus a rank-64 correction at a given layer is effectively something like W2.5. The fair comparison is therefore **W3 SHARQ at equivalent footprint**, not plain W2. Any evaluation that reports "W2 + low-rank" against "W2 baseline" will be correctly torn apart by reviewers. Report effective bits-per-weight explicitly.

