## Part 13 — Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **SHARQ** | SHift-Add Routed Quantization |
| **PE** | Processing element — one MAC unit in the systolic array |
| **BoA** | Best-of-All, Samsung Labs' PTQ framework; SHARQ's backbone |
| **PTQ** | Post-training quantization |
| **W4A16** | 4-bit weights, FP16 activations |
| **Legal family** | The 11 magnitudes `{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,8,9,10,12}` — the popcount-≤2 subset of UINT4 |
| **Tier-1 level** | One shift term; adder bypassed, second path gated |
| **Tier-2 level** | Two shift terms; adder active |
| **Tier-0/1/2 hardware** | Hardwired / mode-selected / fully programmable table (different axis — see §3.7) |
| **Enable table** | The register bank holding code→routing entries. Stores routing, not values. |
| **Exponent adder** | 5-bit add into the FP16 exponent field. Formerly (badly) called a "shifter". |
| **Group scale α** | Per-group FP16 scale, applied once per group outside the inner loop |
| **Oracle-first ladder** | Build the strongest selector first, constrain downward, measure the toll |
| **Palette** | 4 codebooks per layer, channels route to one (ladder rung R3) |
| **Reclaimed −0** | Remapping the redundant sign-magnitude negative-zero code to an extra level |
| **MixPE** | arXiv:2411.16158 — the key competitor and structural template |
| **B1** | The pending single-PE synthesis run; current critical path |

